@page "/source"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]
@inject RestaurantOptions Options

@* The source offer (TECHNICAL_SPECIFICATION §11.9, F-39). Reached from the colophon in the footer of
   every page, in both layouts.

   WHAT IT DISCHARGES. AGPL-3.0-only §13: a modified version "must prominently offer all users
   interacting with it remotely through a computer network ... an opportunity to receive the
   Corresponding Source of your version by providing access to the Corresponding Source from a
   network server at no charge, through some standard or customary means of facilitating copying of
   software." A link to a public repository is the customary means; naming the revision is what makes
   it an offer of *this* version rather than of something adjacent to it.

   The obligation binds whoever modifies the Program, not whoever merely runs it — so an unmodified
   deployment of this tree owes nothing and this page is a courtesy. Shipping it anyway means an
   operator who forks complies by setting RESTAURANT_SOURCE_URL, rather than by discovering §13 after
   somebody asks.

   ANONYMOUS AND STATIC SSR, on purpose. Anonymous because "all users interacting with it remotely"
   includes a guest who never signs in and a tablet that never will; static SSR because a page that
   needed a circuit would be blank on exactly the surfaces least likely to have one. It is also on
   §3.5's exemption list, so a person the obligations pipeline has otherwise locked to one page can
   still read the licence offer — the pipeline exists to stop them *acting*, not to stop them reading
   what the software is.

   The revision is rendered as text rather than composed into a link. Building "{url}/tree/{revision}"
   would be this page guessing at the URL layout of a forge it has never been told the identity of;
   GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, cgit and Sourcehut do not agree on that path, and a link that 404s is worse
   than a hash somebody can paste into `git checkout`. *@

<PageTitle>Source code — @Options.RestaurantName</PageTitle>

<section class="panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free software</p>
    <h1>Source code</h1>

    <p class="lede">
        This site runs <strong>MyRestaurant</strong>, a self-hosted restaurant ordering system
        published under the <strong>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only</strong>. You are
        free to run it, study it, modify it, and share it — and anyone who runs a modified copy as a
        network service owes its users that same freedom.
    </p>

    <dl class="source-facts">
        <dt>Version</dt>
        <dd>@_version</dd>

        <dt>Source revision</dt>
        <dd>
            @if (_hasRevision)
            {
                <code class="source-revision">@_revision</code>
            }
            else
            {
                <span class="source-unknown">
                    Not recorded. This build was produced without a revision stamp, so it can be
                    identified by its version only.
                </span>
            }
        </dd>

        <dt>Licence</dt>
        <dd>AGPL-3.0-only</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Where to get it</h2>

    <p>
        The operator of this instance publishes the corresponding source at:
    </p>

    <p class="source-link">
        <a href="@Options.SourceUrl" rel="external noopener" target="_blank">@Options.SourceUrl</a>
    </p>

    @if (_hasRevision)
    {
        <p class="source-hint">
            To obtain exactly the version you are interacting with, check out revision
            <code class="source-revision">@_revision</code> from that repository.
        </p>
    }

    <p class="source-hint">
        If this site has been modified and the link above does not lead to those modifications, that is
        a licence problem rather than a preference — tell whoever operates it.
    </p>
</section>

@code {
    private string _version = string.Empty;
    private string _revision = string.Empty;
    private bool _hasRevision;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        BuildInformation build = BuildInformation.Current;

        _version = build.Version;
        _hasRevision = build.HasSourceRevision;

        // The full revision here, not the abbreviated one the colophon shows: this is the page whose
        // job is to be pasted into `git checkout`, and seven characters is a convenience rather than
        // an identifier.
        _revision = build.SourceRevision ?? string.Empty;
    }
}
